      formula: "Framework: migration can be driven by political and legal change as well as by land hunger.",
      substitution: "The new British policies removed the Boers' labour system and favoured the natives.",
      calculation: "Losing their slaves and facing equality with blacks led the Boers to seek land and freedom elsewhere.",
      answer: "The Boers trekked north as a reaction to the freedom law and to the new ideas of equality between blacks and whites."
